uiug.30112026470077"}],"summary":"See complete record at pointer"}],"notice":"Research startup packet; statuses remain provisional. Overflow records are explicit and require their source pointers.","overflow":{"claim_draft":{"reason":"30 KB startup budget; follow record pointers for complete evidence","sha256":"765237d14f17f6755b3aa9217fbbc0030f0a97da40152d1695c0fd62c230485d"},"conflicts":{"reason":"30 KB startup budget; follow record pointers for complete evidence","sha256":"382f227256dc45d7196bdd386ee1275926be17845762d9538c027f6c1040f77a"},"current_law_hits":{"reason":"30 KB startup budget; follow record pointers for complete evidence","sha256":"4f53cda18c2baa0c0354bb5f9a3ecbe5ed12ab4d8e11ba873c2f11161202b945"},"fragments":{"reason":"30 KB startup budget; follow record pointers for complete evidence","sha256":"143c4ffd483470abfe5dcd73c6385af9bc0958f85ee8036640134b243097faaf"},"later_events":{"reason":"30 KB startup budget; follow record pointers for complete evidence","sha256":"e91e6969d9376b09deedf36e6fc2299bd2ed5eef616981b146abeb0a159b7d16"}},"readiness":{"blockers":"NO_CLAUSE_INVENTORY|FIRST_END_UNPROVED|SAVINGS_RESIDUALS_NOT_CLOSED|QUARANTINED_RELATIONSHIP_CONFLICT","claim_present":"no","claim_record_errors":"","decision_origin":"inherited_legacy_v2","exhausted_steps":"","instrument_id":"EO:10560","provisional_status":"no","ready_for_human_review":"no","ready_tier":"","step_clause_inventory":"open","step_counterevidence":"open","step_ending_or_current_basis":"open","step_opus_media":"n/a","step_original_text":"done","step_provisional_status":"done","step_savings_residuals":"open","step_shared_sources":"n/a","steps_applicable":"6","steps_done":"2"},"readiness_blockers":[{"step":"clause_inventory","what":"no clause inventory drafted; clause-drafts could not segment the available text(s): official_fr_scan_ocr_text:segmented:unusable(section_number_gap_1->3,4->6;text_contains_contents_listing_fragments_columns_may_be_interleaved;incomplete_section_markers_not_split_2;incomplete_clause_o"}],"schema":"eo-case-bundle/v1","status":"no","text_pointers":[{"first_1500_characters":"{\"member\": \"usc02.xml\", \"note_id\": \"iddcb8117d-3a6e-11f1-a0f3-db3efcbbb4ee\", \"citation\": \"2 U.S.C. 685 note\", \"heading\": \"Ex. Ord. No. 11845. Delegation of Certain Reporting Functions to Director of Office of Management and Budget\", \"subjects\": [\"11845\"], \"status_line\": \"Ex. Ord. No. 11845, Mar. 24, 1975, 40 F.R. 13299, as amended by Ex. Ord. No. 12608, Sept. 9, 1987, 52 F.R. 34617, provided:\", \"text\": \"Ex. Ord. No. 11845. Delegation of Certain Reporting Functions to Director of Office of Management and Budget\\nEx. Ord. No. 11845, Mar. 24, 1975, 40 F.R. 13299, as amended by Ex. Ord. No. 12608, Sept. 9, 1987, 52 F.R. 34617, provided:\\nBy virtue of the authority vested in me by the Impoundment Control Act of 1974 (Public Law 93–344; 88 Stat. 332, (2 U.S.C. 681 et seq.), hereinafter referred to as the Act) [subchapters I and II of this chapter], and section 301 of title 3 of the United States Code, the Director of the Office of Management and Budget is hereby designated and empowered to exercise, as of October 1, 1974 without ratification or other action of the President (1) the functions required by sections 1014(b) and 1014(d) of the Act [subsecs. (b) and (d) of this section] of transmitting to the Comptroller General of the United States and to the Office of the Federal Register copies of special messages transmitted pursuant to section 1012 or 1013 (2 U.S.C. 683 and 684) of the Act; and (2) the function conferred upon the President by section 1014(e) of the Act (2 U.S.C. 685","path":"jobs/current-law/output/USC_EO_NOTES.jsonl","sha256":"ac1e287b6b606b8adc5c1975f662aae2d31989c1d072e32c89dbc38f6efe8016","source":{"line":3,"path":"jobs/current-law/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"5b6e5de61be4ea9c9c4749827c02d0c9d484107505b7e9adae3172a42351c188"}},{"first_1500_characters":"Instrument: EO:10560\nSource: https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1954-09-14/pdf/FR-1954-09-14.pdf\nSHA-256 of the downloaded file: 19f6c75ad0e3300b8634bbe4a80f137375704244ed193a9a08914638ef9d2a08\nLocation: 19 FR 5927, PDF pages 1-3 (confidence high)\nMachine-extracted text layer of the official PDF (OCR for 1936-1994 scans). May contain recognition errors and parts of neighbouring documents on the same pages. Not an authenticated transcription: check the PDF pages.\n\n=== PDF page 1 of 36 ===\nEDERALESISTER\nVOLUME 19 ^ O N n t O ^ NUMBER 178\nWashington, Tuesday, September 14, 1954\nTITLE 3— THE PRESIDENT\nEXECUTIVE ORDER 10560\nAdministration  of the A gricultural\nT rade D evelopment  and A ssistance\nAct of 1954\nBy virtue of the authority vested in \nme by section 301 of title 3 of the United \nStates Code, 65 Stat. 713, and as Presi­\ndent of the United States, it is ordered \nas follows:\nSection  1. Department of Agriculture.  \nExcept as otherwise provided in this \norder, the functions conferred upon the \nPresident by Title I  of the Agricultural \nTrade Development and Assistance Act \nof 1954 are hereby delegated to the Sec­\nretary of Agriculture. ~\nSec. 2. Foreign Operations Adminis­\ntration.  The functions conferred upon \nthe President by Title n  of the Act are \nhereby delegated to the Director of the \nForeign Operations Administration.\nSec. 3. Department of State,  (a) The \nfunctions of negotiating and entering \ninto agreements with friendly nations or \norganizations of friendly","path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/texts/EO_10560.txt","sha256":"a649524ba07436f8b683dfc6065dfbd14c0d983f5cbbf68bec7dcfb40cd2142b","source":{"line":803,"path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"2a87f807f93a592af1cc2a8297ddbee17766fbe81688d229956b30c3e63fcf89"}}]}
